    "chunk_size_bytes": 1759,
    "chunk_text": "An Act to amend the Rubber Control Act\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows :-\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Rubber Control (Amendment) Act, No. of 2025.\n\n(2) Every reference to the \u201cController\u201d and \u201cRubber Controller\u201d in any other written law or in any notice, notification, contract, communication, form, other instrument or document shall from and after the date of commencement of this Act be read and construed as a reference made to the \u201cDirector-General of the Rubber Development Department\u201d.\n\n3. Section 26 of the principal enactment is hereby repealed.\n\n4. The heading appearing immediately after the words and figures \u201cPART VI\u201d of the principal enactment is hereby repealed and the following heading substituted therefor: -\n\n\u201cRUBBER ADVISORY BOARD\u201d.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\nReplacement of heading in Part VI of the principal enactment\n\nRubber Control (Amendment)2\n\n5. Sections 36, 37, 38, 39, 39a and 50 of the principal enactment are hereby repealed.\n\n6. Section 52 of the principal enactment is hereby amended by the repeal of the definition of \u201cController\u201d, and the substitution therefor, of the following new definition :-\n\n\u201c\u201cDirector-General\u201d means the Director-General of the Rubber Development Department, appointed or deemed to have been appointed under this Act;\u201d.\n\n7. In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhala and Tamil texts of this Act the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\n5\n\n10\n\nRepeal of sections 36, 37, 38, 39, 39a and 50 of the principal enactment\n\nAmendment of section 52 of the principal enactment\n\nSinhala text toprevail in caseof inconsistency\n\n3Rubber Control (Amendment)\n\nRubber Control (Amendment)4\n\nDEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING"
